# Rose and Thorn's ghosts in the attic children's room (death_house_attic). They don't know they are dead.
# Choices: tell them gently or plainly, let them ride along inside the party, or promise to carry their bones to
# the family crypt. Leaving them, or a hard truth, makes Thorn try to climb inside someone.

~ start
if flag.death_house_children_met
  -> again
endif
set death_house_children_met
quest rose_and_thorn met
Narrator: Two children sit on the floor beside a dollhouse, pale as frost on a window. The girl looks up first, with a hope that has had a long time to get thin.
if flag.death_house_heard_plea
  Narrator: You know these faces: they begged you for help in the road outside. These two have been here much longer.
endif
Rose [afraid]: Is it over? Is the noise over? Mother said she'd unlock the door when the noise downstairs stopped.
Thorn: You're not Mother.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: No! No. Friends. Of the family, sort of. Would you like an apricot? Can you... no. Sorry. Hello.
if not name:kip_smudgewick
  interject tag:cheerful: Hello there. No, we're not your mother. We're the next best thing. Probably.
endif
-> ask

~ ask
* Who locked you in? -> locked
* [if flag.death_house_heard_plea] You asked us to save Walter. Outside, in the road. -> outside
* Where is Walter? -> walter
* [Insight DC 12] Do they know what's happened to them? -> know_ok | know_fail
* [if not flag.death_house_children_truth] Tell them the truth: they died in this room. -> truth
* [if flag.death_house_children_truth] Come with us, then. Stay close. -> ride_along
* [if flag.death_house_children_truth and not flag.death_house_children_remains_taken] We'll carry your bones to your crypt. -> promise_bones
* We have to go. Stay here. -> leaving

~ locked
Rose: Mother and Father. The people in robes mustn't see us, they said, and we mustn't see them. They'd come back up when it was over.
Thorn: They didn't.
Rose [angry]: They will. Mother promised.
-> ask

~ outside
Rose [afraid]: Outside? We haven't been outside since the leaves were green. Mother won't let us.
Thorn: Was it us? Was it really us?
Narrator: Somewhere in the walls a board creaks, slow and satisfied, like a fisherman reeling in a line.
if not flag.death_house_saw_through_lure
  set death_house_saw_through_lure
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
-> ask

~ walter
Rose: He was with Nurse. Then he wasn't, and Nurse cried, and then Nurse stopped crying.
Thorn: Downstairs. Everybody goes downstairs.
-> ask

~ know_ok
Narrator: They don't know; they are still waiting for a door to open, the way you wait for morning. Telling them will hurt, and not telling them will hurt longer.
-> ask

~ know_fail
Narrator: Two stubborn, frightened faces. {name} can't read past that.
-> ask

~ truth
Narrator: How do you tell a child she is dead?
* [Persuasion DC 12] Gently: kneel, take your time, let them ask. Rush it and Thorn may panic. -> truth_gentle | truth_hard
* [Cleric] [Religion DC 10] With the prayer for the dead, as for any family. Stumble and Thorn may panic. -> truth_gentle | truth_hard
* Plainly. They deserve the truth. -> truth_hard
* Not yet. -> ask

~ truth_gentle
Narrator: Rose listens all the way through. When it's over she looks down at her hands, as if she has only now noticed she can see the floor through them.
Rose [sad]: Oh. That's why we're never hungry anymore.
Thorn: Are we in trouble?
Rose: No, Thorn. I think everyone else is.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +2 kip_smudgewick +1: You told the Durst children the truth, gently
-> truth_learned

~ truth_learned
if not flag.death_house_children_truth
  set death_house_children_truth
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
Rose: We hid in the toy chest when it got cold. Our bones are still there. Our crypts are downstairs, by Grandmother's. Mother showed us.
Rose [sad]: Will you take us?
interject name:thistle: Course we will. You're mine now. Both of you.
if not name:thistle
  interject class:cleric: Yes. That much, at least, we can do properly.
endif
-> ask

~ truth_hard
Narrator: Thorn hears the word and doesn't understand it. Then he does.
Thorn [angry]: No! You're lying! You're going to leave us, like they did!
Narrator: The room drops cold enough to hurt, and the boy flings himself at the nearest of you.
check Charisma DC 12 -> thorn_resisted | thorn_rides

~ thorn_resisted
Narrator: He breaks against a will that won't let him in and falls back, sobbing, into his sister's arms.
Rose [afraid]: He's frightened. We both are. Please don't leave us.
-> truth_learned

~ thorn_rides
Narrator: He goes into one of you like breath into a cold mirror; for a moment two sets of eyes look out of the same face, then only one. Somewhere inside, a small boy stops crying.
Rose [angry]: Thorn! Come out of there! ...Fine. Then I'm coming too.
Narrator: She steps into another of you, apologizing as she goes. Now someone in the party is humming a nursery tune that none of you started.
set death_house_children_riding
if not flag.death_house_children_truth
  set death_house_children_truth
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Right. One of us has a lodger. Hands up? Nobody? Lovely.
-> END

~ ride_along
Rose: Hold still. It doesn't hurt. Thorn, say sorry first.
Thorn: Sorry first.
Narrator: Two cold presences step inside two of you and settle, the way children settle in the back of a cart. Someone is humming now, and none of you started it.
set death_house_children_riding
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Two more for the party, then. Welcome, both of you. Hold on tight; I'm very tall.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +2 wren_featherfoot +1 thistle +1: You let two dead children ride along with you
-> END

~ promise_bones
Rose [smile]: You'll have to undo the knot. Thorn tied it. It's a bad knot.
Thorn: It's a good knot.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +2 liriel_dawnsong +2: You promised to carry the children's bones to their crypt
-> END

~ leaving
if flag.death_house_children_truth
  Rose [sad]: Everyone says that. Come back. Please come back.
  -> END
endif
Thorn [angry]: Don't go! Everybody goes!
Narrator: The boy flings himself at the nearest of you before anyone can move.
check Charisma DC 12 -> leave_resisted | thorn_rides

~ leave_resisted
Narrator: He bounces off a will like a bird off a window and sits down hard, wailing. Rose holds him and glares at you over his head.
Rose [angry]: Go on, then. Everybody does.
-> END

~ again
Rose [smile]: You came back!
Thorn: Told you.
-> ask
